                <td width=572 valign=center colspan=10 style="width:343.6000pt;padding:0.0000pt 5.4000pt 0.0000pt 5.4000pt ;border-left:none;
mso-border-left-alt:none;border-right:1.0000pt solid windowtext;mso-border-right-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;
border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;border-bottom:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">As a key bridge between basic medicine and oral clinic, this course includes three initial parts of stomatology: oral embryology, oral histology and oral pathology. The course is after learning-centered revolution by using artificial intelligence and online and offline mixed approach. Through the whole course, students can achieve such goals: (1) understand the normal tissue structure and pathological changes of oral and maxillofacial region, (2) cultivate the abilities of spatial imagination, image recognition and critical thinking, (3) make pathological diagnosis of common oral diseases, (4) establish the logical thinking of disease dynamic development, and (5) stimulate the interest in subject exploration.</span></p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
